# Frontend standards

Canonical detail: `AGENTS.md`.

- Prefer TypeScript, typed boundaries, and the existing layout of the frontend workspace when one exists.
- Do not invent latency, cost, or quality numbers in the UI; display only values the backend actually returned.
- Do not log secrets, tokens, or personal data to the browser console in production paths.
- Before finishing: run the project's typecheck and build (for example `npm run typecheck` and `npm run build` from the frontend workspace).
- Do not add a separate frontend CI workflow unless the project has already outgrown the default jobs.
